<%# The bar an original in the archive wears: the way back to the archive, and
    nothing else. Held mail wears the pen's bar instead.

    It pointed at the reader until the reader was deleted. Where back goes now
    depends on where the mail lives rather than on where the reader came from:
    the archive for content, the pen for a dismissed confirmation, which
    Newsletter.content keeps off the archive while the new-senders list still
    links to it. The presenter owns that choice and the label with it. %>
<header class="topbar">
  <%= link_to newsletter.back_label,
        newsletter.back_path,
        class: "topbar__back" %>
</header>
